MARKETING CLAIMS - AUTUMN/WINTER 2026
Sustainability and environmental claims proposed for AW26 copy, with the evidence held for each

CLAIM 1: "Made from 100% recycled materials" (footwear)
- Evidence: recycled-content certificate covers the outsole and laces only; uppers are virgin synthetic

CLAIM 2: "Carbon neutral shipping" (accessories)
- Evidence: carbon offset purchases for the freight emissions; offsets are not independently verified and no reduction plan exists

CLAIM 3: "Organic cotton sourced" (apparel)
- Evidence: organic certificates (GOTS) cover about 60% of cotton volume; transaction certificates for the rest are missing

CLAIM 4: "Sustainable production certified" (apparel)
- Evidence: none. No certification scheme is named and no certificate is on file

CLAIM 5: "Fair trade partner" (footwear)
- Evidence: Fairtrade licence numbers held for the named suppliers

CLAIM 6: "Plastic-free packaging" (accessories)
- Evidence: supplier declarations only; polybags are still used for inner packing on two lines

CLAIM 7: "Zero waste manufacturing" (footwear)
- Evidence: none. Factory waste data shows offcuts sent to landfill at two of the footwear factories

REGULATORY CONTEXT:
UK ASA Code requires substantiation for all claims
CMA Green Claims Code covers carbon and environmental claims
EU rules on green claims are becoming more stringent
